::MLA.ENG1.C.02 U06 L04 GP Q01::Digital presentation purpose: Explain how weekly planning helps students manage assignments. Which slide should come first? {
~A. A final thank-you slide#Incorrect. A thank-you slide belongs at the end, not before the audience knows the perspective.
=B. A slide stating the topic and clear perspective#Correct. A digital presentation should begin by orienting the audience to the main idea.
~C. A random image of a backpack#Incorrect. An image without purpose does not establish coherent ideas.
~D. A list of unrelated homework complaints#Incorrect. This does not introduce a clear presentation focus.
}

::MLA.ENG1.R.05 U06 L04 GP Q02::Presentation purpose: Show a problem and then recommend a solution. Which structure fits best? {
~A. Compare-contrast#Incorrect. Compare-contrast is for similarities and differences, not mainly problem and solution.
~B. Random order#Incorrect. Random order weakens coherence.
=C. Problem-solution#Correct. This structure matches a presentation that identifies a problem and recommends a solution.
~D. Alphabetical order#Incorrect. Alphabetical order usually does not build meaning for this purpose.
}

::MLA.ENG1.C.02 U06 L04 GP Q03::Which slide sequence is most coherent? {
~A. Funny image, thank-you slide, problem, title#Incorrect. This order confuses the audience and delays the focus.
=D. Title and perspective, problem, solution, final takeaway#Correct. This sequence builds a clear idea in logical order.
~C. Solution, unrelated quote, title, random fact#Incorrect. This sequence does not develop one coherent idea.
~B. Final takeaway, title, unrelated image, problem#Incorrect. The final takeaway should not appear before the audience understands the presentation.
}

::MLA.ENG1.W.03 U06 L04 GP Q04::Which slide note best fits an expository digital presentation? {
=A. Step 1: Identify all due dates for the week.#Correct. This note clearly explains one step in an organized process.
~B. Due dates are annoying and nobody likes them.#Incorrect. This is informal and not explanatory.
~C. I do not know what the next slide is about.#Incorrect. This shows lack of organization.
~D. Look at this unrelated picture.#Incorrect. This does not explain information.
}

::MLA.ENG1.C.02 U06 L04 GP Q05::A digital presentation has slides about planning, cafeteria menus, sports scores, and homework. What is the main issue? {
~A. It has too few colors.#Incorrect. The main issue is not design color.
~B. It uses no paragraphs.#Incorrect. Slides should not rely on long paragraphs.
=C. It lacks coherent ideas because the slides do not support one perspective.#Correct. The topics are disconnected and do not build one clear message.
~D. It needs more unrelated slides.#Incorrect. More unrelated slides would make coherence worse.
}
